<!-- FreeSWITCH SIP gateway — Jio Enterprise SIP trunk (circuit-delivered) -->
<include>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    JIO ENTERPRISE SIP TRUNK

    Provisioning (Adexos Global Technologies):
      Circuit    SIP_9188875079_8633502031
      Channels   10 concurrent
      Our IP     100.65.188.4   (on the Jio circuit, /28 pool)
      Gateway    100.65.188.1
      Jio SBC    100.64.0.4     (signalling)
      Jio media  100.64.0.6     (RTP)
      DIDs       8633502031 - 8633502064   (34 numbers, 10-digit)

    AUTH: IP-based. Jio supplied no SIP username or password — the
    circuit itself is the credential, and their SBC authorises us by
    source IP. So register is FALSE. Setting it true would loop on
    FAIL_WAIT forever against an SBC that never expects a REGISTER,
    which reads exactly like a wrong-password problem and wastes days.
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <gateway name="jio_primary">
    <!-- No credentials: IP-authenticated trunk -->
    <param name="register"               value="false"/>
    <param name="proxy"                  value="100.64.0.4"/>
    <param name="realm"                  value="100.64.0.4"/>
    <param name="from-domain"            value="100.65.188.4"/>
    <!-- OPTIONS ping keeps the path warm and makes trunk death visible
         in `sofia status gateway` instead of at the next real call. -->
    <param name="ping"                   value="30"/>
    <param name="ping-max"               value="3"/>
    <param name="caller-id-in-from"      value="true"/>
    <param name="context"                value="heynikki"/>
    <!-- G.711 only. The pipeline cannot decode G.729 — if Jio offers
         it, decline rather than negotiate it. -->
    <param name="codec-prefs"            value="PCMU,PCMA"/>
    <!-- Jio sold 10 channels. A sofia gateway has NO channel-cap
         parameter — this comment claimed a cap that did not exist here,
         and call eleven was refused by Jio's SBC as a generic
         NORMAL_TEMPORARY_FAILURE, indistinguishable from a dead trunk.
         The cap now lives where it can be counted: esl.ts asks
         `show channels count` before every originate and stops outbound
         at TRUNK_OUTBOUND_CEILING (8 of 10), leaving two channels for
         people ringing in. This is the rate limit, which is a different
         thing and does belong here. -->
    <param name="calls-per-second"       value="3"/>
  </gateway>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    VI BUSINESS FAILOVER — not purchased. Deliberately absent so it
    cannot spam registration failures that mask real Jio errors.
    The dialplan bridges "jio_primary|vi_failover" and FreeSWITCH
    simply skips a gateway that isn't defined.
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

</include>
